{
  "id": "1CH.1",
  "number": "1",
  "bookId": "1CH",
  "reference": "1 Chronicles 1",
  "verseCount": 43,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "1",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "1CH 1"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "1",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Adam was the father of Seth, Seth was the father of Enosh, Enosh the father of Kenan, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Kenan the father of Mahalalel, Mahalalel the father of Jared. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Jared was the father of Enoch, who was the father of Methuselah; Methuselah was the father of Lamech, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "who was the father of Noah. Noah had three sons: Shem, Ham, and Japheth.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.4"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The sons of Japheth — Gomer, Magog, Madai, Javan, Tubal, Meshech, and Tiras — were the ancestors of the peoples who bear their names. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The descendants of Gomer were the people of Ashkenaz, Riphath, and Togarmah. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The descendants of Javan were the people of Elishah, Spain, Cyprus, and Rhodes.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.7"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The sons of Ham — Cush, Egypt, Libya, and Canaan — were the ancestors of the peoples who bear their names. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The descendants of Cush were the people of Seba, Havilah, Sabtah, Raamah, and Sabteca. The descendants of Raamah were the people of Sheba and Dedan. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "(Cush had a son named Nimrod, who became the world's first great conqueror.) ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The descendants of Egypt were the people of Lydia, Anam, Lehab, Naphtuh, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pathrus, Casluh, and of Crete (from whom the Philistines were descended). ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Canaan's sons — Sidon, the eldest, and Heth — were the ancestors of the peoples who bear their names. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Canaan was also the ancestor of the Jebusites, the Amorites, Girgashites, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Hivites, Arkites, Sinites, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Arvadites, Zemarites, and Hamathites.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.16"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Shem's sons — Elam, Asshur, Arpachshad, Lud, Aram, Uz, Hul, Gether, and Meshek — were the ancestors of the peoples who bear their names. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Arpachshad was the father of Shelah, who was the father of Eber. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Eber had two sons; one was named Peleg,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1.19",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Peleg",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": ": This name sounds like the Hebrew for “divide”.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " because during his time the people of the world were divided, and the other was named Joktan. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The descendants of Joktan were the people of Almodad, Sheleph, Hazarmaveth, Jerah, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Hadoram, Uzal, Diklah, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ebal, Abimael, Sheba, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ophir, Havilah, and Jobab.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.23"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The family line from Shem to Abram is as follows: Shem, Arpachshad, Shelah, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Eber, Peleg, Reu, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Serug, Nahor, Terah, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and Abram (also known as Abraham).",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.27"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.27"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Abraham had two sons, Isaac and Ishmael. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The sons of Ishmael became the heads of twelve tribes: Nebaioth (from the name of Ishmael's eldest son), Kedar, Adbeel, Mibsam, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.29"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "30",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:30"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Mishma, Dumah, Massa, Hadad, Tema, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "31",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:31"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "31",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Jetur, Naphish, and Kedemah.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.31"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "31",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:31"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "31",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.31"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "32",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:32"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "32",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Abraham had a concubine named Keturah, who bore him six sons: Zimran, Jokshan, Medan, Midian, Ishbak, and Shuah. Jokshan had two sons: Sheba and Dedan. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.32"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "33",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 1:33"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "33",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Midian had five sons: Ephah, Epher, Hanoch, Abida, and Eldaah.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.1.33",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.1.33"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
